Return `false` from the `_.transform` callback to stop iteration early:

```js
const result = _.transform([2, 3, 4], (accumulator, n) => {
  accumulator.push(n * n);
  return n % 2 === 0; // false stops iteration
}, []);

// result: [4, 9]
```

The callback receives `(accumulator, value, key, object)`. Mutate the accumulator, then return `false` when you want iteration to end.
